00:04:25.441 --> 00:04:26.948
Security

00:04:27.856 --> 00:04:30.751
The usual way routine creative work gets

00:04:30.815 --> 00:04:34.872
done is a liability surface: files emailed

00:04:34.963 --> 00:04:38.041
to outside contractors, brand assets

00:04:38.105 --> 00:04:41.450
uploaded to a dozen web editors, customer

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:44.650
data pasted into a stranger's site to make

00:04:44.708 --> 00:04:46.395
a quick graphic.

00:04:47.188 --> 00:04:49.803
Lolly is the immune response to that,

00:04:49.861 --> 00:04:52.254
because it replaces the work rather than

00:04:52.339 --> 00:04:55.619
adding a control on top of it: the quote

00:04:55.679 --> 00:04:58.211
card, the localised banner and the

00:04:58.271 --> 00:05:00.496
redacted screenshot are made on the

00:05:00.552 --> 00:05:03.669
employee's own device against your brand,

00:05:03.747 --> 00:05:06.151
so nothing uploads that you did not put

00:05:06.211 --> 00:05:08.809
there and every result is reproducible

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.595
from its inputs.

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:13.421
Exports can carry several layers of

00:05:13.481 --> 00:05:16.663
cryptographic record - a C2PA Content

00:05:16.722 --> 00:05:19.164
Credential signed by a key generated on

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:21.989
the device and never readable off it, the

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.460
invisible Lolly Imprint and an opt-in

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:26.840
durable mark that outlives a re-save -

00:05:26.899 --> 00:05:28.877
each of which is tamper-evident and

00:05:28.932 --> 00:05:31.898
strippable: a credential flags a change

00:05:31.959 --> 00:05:34.503
rather than preventing one, and that is

00:05:34.563 --> 00:05:36.817
precisely what makes fully offline

00:05:36.877 --> 00:05:38.332
verification

00:05:39.173 --> 00:05:40.417
possible.

00:05:41.184 --> 00:05:43.875
The cryptography and the file parsers are

00:05:43.935 --> 00:05:46.155
going through SUSE's enterprise-grade

00:05:46.215 --> 00:05:49.635
hardening: the seals, on-device signing

00:05:49.712 --> 00:05:52.204
and encryption are real and defensible

00:05:52.263 --> 00:05:55.187
now, so where a contract calls for

00:05:55.282 --> 00:05:58.056
certified assurance, deploy them as

00:05:58.116 --> 00:06:00.221
defence-in-depth while that process

00:06:00.281 --> 00:06:01.545
completes.

